window.NTI=window.NTI||{};(window.NTI.docs=window.NTI.docs||{})["ansible-30-production-br-ansible"]={"html":"ANSIBLE PRODUCTION — FROM MARKDOWN, FULL DETAIL<div class=\"sheet cover\"><div class=\"ckick\">Automation Control Manual</div><div class=\"stamp\">ANSIBLE</div><h1 id=\"productionansible\">PRODUCTION<br />ANSIBLE</h1><hr /><div class=\"sub\">Secure, Tested and Delivered — <b>Vol 3</b><br />Full chapter detail — rendered from content Markdown</div><div class=\"vols\"><div class=\"volcard\">VOL 1 — FOUNDATIONS</div><div class=\"volcard\">VOL 2 — ENGINEERING</div><div class=\"volcard on\">VOL 3 — PRODUCTION<small>this book</small></div></div><div class=\"cver\">A4 · Playwright · Background ON · Eye Palette · Rendered from content Markdown · production</div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Contents</div><h1 id=\"table-of-contents\">TABLE OF CONTENTS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">CORE</span></div></div><div><div><a href=\"#ch-10\"><span class=\"tnum\">10</span><span class=\"tp\">Security and Vault</span><span class=\"dots\"></span>03</a><a href=\"#ch-11\"><span class=\"tnum\">11</span><span class=\"tp\">Testing and Quality</span><span class=\"dots\"></span>10</a></div><div><a href=\"#ch-12\"><span class=\"tnum\">12</span><span class=\"tp\">CI/CD and Production</span><span class=\"dots\"></span>14</a><a href=\"#ch-13\"><span class=\"tnum\">13</span><span class=\"tp\">Advanced Automation</span><span class=\"dots\"></span>21</a><a href=\"#cheatsheet\"><span class=\"tnum\">A</span><span class=\"tp\">Cheatsheet</span><span class=\"dots\"></span>25</a></div></div><div class=\"mark m-key\"><span class=\"tag\">How to read</span>Chapters render the full content Markdown: secrets, quality gates, delivery, recovery, labs, interview checks.</div><p>Version anchor: Same pins as Vol 1 (core 2.16+, lint 6+, molecule 6+); vault secrets via prompt, file or CI..</p><div class=\"panel\"><div class=\"ptitle\">Production loop — every push</div><div class=\"frow\"><span class=\"blk b-red\">VAULT</span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk\">LINT + TEST</span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk b-chg\">CI/CD ROLLING</span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk b-ok\">OBSERVE</span></div></div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">2</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 10 · Security</div><h1 id=\"vault-become-secrets\">VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHAT — Least privilege + encrypted secrets</div><p><code>become</code> escalates privilege (typically sudo) per play, role, or task. Ansible Vault encrypts variables and files so secrets live in Git safely and decrypt only at run time.</p><div class=\"panel\"><div class=\"zlabel\">Secrets stay encrypted until run time</div><div class=\"frow\"><span class=\"blk\">PLAINTEXT VAR</span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk b-chg\">VAULT ENCRYPT</span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk\">COMMIT SAFE</span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk b-ok\">DECRYPT AT RUN</span></div></div><div class=\"code\">- name: Configure web fleet\n  hosts: web\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  vars_files:\n    - group_vars/prod/vault.yml\n  tasks:\n    - name: Deploy TLS key\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        src: tls.key\n        dest: /etc/nginx/tls.key\n        mode: '0600'</div><div class=\"code\">ansible-vault encrypt group_vars/prod/vault.yml\nansible-playbook -i inventory.ini site.yml --ask-vault-pass</div><p>Vault file holds <code>vault_tls_key</code>, <code>vault_db_password</code> — referenced as <code>{{ vault_db_password }}</code>, never in plain vars.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">WHY — Automation is a privileged secret-spreader</div><p>Playbooks run as root across fleets and touch credentials. Plain-text secrets in Git leak to every clone; blanket <code>become: true</code> with passwordless sudo everywhere widens blast radius. Vault + scoped become give two guarantees: secrets encrypted at rest in version control, privilege granted narrowly per task.</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">3</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 10 · Security (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"vault-become-secrets-2\">VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHERE DOES IT FIT — Secure after organize</div><div class=\"code\">Roles/collections (Ch 09) define vars → Vault encrypts the sensitive subset → become scopes who applies them\n  → testing (Ch 11) verifies without leaking → CI/CD (Ch 12) injects vault password from CI secrets</div><p>Do not confuse Ansible Vault (file/var encryption in-repo) with HashiCorp Vault (external secret store via lookup plugins). They compose: external vault supplies at run, Ansible Vault encrypts what must live in Git.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">HOW IT WORKS — Encrypt, scope, inject</div><p>Vault: <code>ansible-vault encrypt|decrypt|view|edit|rekey</code> per file; <code>encrypt_string</code> for inline values. Multiple vault IDs (<code>--vault-id prod@prompt</code>) separate environments. At run, password comes from prompt, file (<code>--vault-password-file</code>), or CI secret → file. <code>no_log: true</code> on secret-touching tasks suppresses output.</p><p>Become: <code>become: true</code> + <code>become_user</code> + <code>become_method: sudo</code> (or <code>su</code>, <code>runas</code> on Windows). Scope narrowly: play default <code>become: false</code>, escalate only tasks needing root. <code>--ask-become-pass</code> for interactive sudo password; in CI use NOPASSWD scoped sudoers or ephemeral privilege.</p><div class=\"code\">- name: Read app status as app user\n  ansible.builtin.command: systemctl --user status app\n  become: true\n  become_user: app\n  register: app_status\n  changed_when: false\n  no_log: false</div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">4</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 10 · Security (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"vault-become-secrets-3\">VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">SUDO PITFALLS — Privilege side: sudoers and become identity</div><p>Most Ansible failures on Linux are not Ansible bugs — they are privilege, ownership, or interpreter mismatches. Learn the five usual suspects.</p><p><b>1. Sudoers scope.</b> Grant the automation user exactly what plays need, nothing more:</p><div class=\"code\">ansible ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl *, /usr/bin/apt-get *, /usr/bin/yum *</div><p>Blanket <code>ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL</code> works in labs and horrifies auditors; passworded sudo needs <code>--ask-become-pass</code> (interactive) or CI-managed credentials. Old RHEL/CentOS images also enforce <code>Defaults requiretty</code> — sudo over non-interactive SSH fails until that line is removed for the automation user.</p><p><b>2. Become identity.</b> <code>become_user</code> decides *who you become*, default <code>root</code>. Database tasks often need the service account instead:</p><div class=\"code\">- name: Vacuum app database\n  community.postgresql.postgresql_query:\n    query: VACUUM ANALYZE\n  become: true\n  become_user: postgres</div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">5</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 10 · Security (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"vault-become-secrets-4\">VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">SUDO PITFALLS — Host side: ownership, SELinux, interpreter</div><p><b>3. Ownership and modes.</b> Files created by a root-run task belong to root. Serve them to an app user and reads fail:</p><div class=\"code\">- name: Deploy app config\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: app.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/app/app.conf\n    owner: app\n    group: app\n    mode: '0640'</div><p>Always set <code>owner/group/mode</code> on security-relevant files; verify with a second task using <code>ansible.builtin.stat</code> when the service is picky.</p><p><b>4. SELinux contexts.</b> On enforcing systems, correct mode with wrong context still denies:</p><div class=\"code\">ansible web -i inventory.ini -m ansible.builtin.command -a \"getenforce\"   # Enforcing?\nansible web -i inventory.ini -m ansible.builtin.command -a \"ls -Z /etc/app/\"</div><p>Fix with <code>community.general.sefcontext</code> + <code>restorecon</code>, or <code>ansible.posix.selinux</code> booleans (<code>httpd_can_network_connect</code> is the classic) — never blanket <code>setenforce 0</code> in production.</p><p><b>5. Python interpreter.</b> Modules execute in Python on the target. Minimal images lack it, or ship two versions:</p><div class=\"code\">[web:vars]\nansible_python_interpreter=/usr/bin/python3</div><p>Symptom <code>MODULE FAILURE: /bin/sh: python: command not found</code> → install <code>python3</code> via a raw bootstrap task (<code>ansible.builtin.raw: apt-get install -y python3</code>) before any module that needs Python. CRLF-edited playbooks from Windows editors also break YAML parsing — keep LF endings (see WSL setup, Ch 02).</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">6</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 10 · Security (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"vault-become-secrets-5\">VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">PRACTICAL — Encrypt and run without leaking</div><div class=\"code\">COMMAND\n────────────────────────\nansible-vault encrypt_string 's3cr3t-db-pass' --name 'vault_db_password'</div><p>Expected: <code>vault_db_password: !vault | $ANSIBLE_VAULT;1.1;AES256...</code> — paste into <code>group_vars/prod/vault.yml</code>, commit safely.</p><div class=\"code\">COMMAND\n────────────────────────\nansible-playbook -i inventory.ini site.yml --ask-vault-pass --check --diff</div><p>Why it matters: proves encrypted vars decrypt at run and dry-run shows structure without exposing values (with <code>no_log: true</code>). Common failure: <code>Attempting to decrypt but no vault secrets found</code> → password file path wrong or <code>--vault-id</code> label mismatch.</p><div class=\"code\">ansible-vault view group_vars/prod/vault.yml      # read without decrypting to disk\nansible-vault edit group_vars/prod/vault.yml      # decrypt, edit, re-encrypt in one step\nansible-vault rekey group_vars/prod/vault.yml     # rotate the password on existing files</div><p><code>view</code> for inspection, <code>edit</code> for changes, <code>rekey</code> for rotation — the file stays encrypted at every step except inside the editor.</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">7</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 10 · Security (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"vault-become-secrets-6\">VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHAT CAN FAIL</div><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely Cause</th><th>Prevention</th></tr><tr><td><code>no vault secrets found</code></td><td>Missing <code>--ask-vault-pass</code> / wrong password file</td><td>CI secret → file → <code>--vault-password-file</code>; test locally with prompt first</td></tr><tr><td><code>Failed to escalate privilege</code></td><td>sudoers denies or password needed</td><td>Scoped NOPASSWD for automation user; <code>--ask-become-pass</code> interactively</td></tr><tr><td>Secret in logs</td><td>Task echoes var without <code>no_log</code></td><td><code>no_log: true</code> on secret tasks; audit with <code>--check -vv</code> in safe env</td></tr><tr><td>Vault + HashiCorp Vault confused</td><td>Same word, different tools</td><td>Ansible Vault = encrypted files in repo; HCP Vault = lookup at run (<code>community.hashi_vault</code>)</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"mark m-warn\"><span class=\"tag\">Gotcha</span>Encrypting a file does not fix over-broad privilege.\nVault protects secrets at rest; become scoping protects hosts at run.\nDo both — one without the other leaves half the attack surface open.</div><div class=\"taskhead\">REAL-WORLD CONNECTION</div><p>TLS key rotation: operator runs <code>ansible-vault rekey</code> per environment file, commits re-encrypted vault, opens PR showing only <code>!vault</code> blobs changed. CI holds vault password as protected secret, runs <code>--check --diff</code> for approval, then applies with <code>serial: 1</code>. Audit trail = Git history of who changed which encrypted file + CI run that decrypted it.</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">8</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 10 · Security (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"vault-become-secrets-7\">VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">LAB — Observe / Execute / Verify</div><p>Objective: secret committed encrypted, applied with scoped privilege. Prereqs: <code>group_vars/prod/vault.yml</code> with one test secret.</p><ol><li><code>ansible-vault encrypt group_vars/prod/vault.yml</code> → Observe blob, <code>git diff</code> shows no plaintext</li><li><code>ansible-vault view group_vars/prod/vault.yml</code> → Verify round-trip decrypt</li><li>Run play with <code>--ask-vault-pass --check --diff</code> → Verify task references <code>{{ vault_db_password }}</code> without printing it (<code>no_log: true</code>)</li><li>Set <code>become: false</code> at play, <code>become: true</code> only on privileged task → Verify least-privilege scoping.</li></ol><p>Failure drill: run without password → decrypt error → add <code>--ask-vault-pass</code> → converges.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">Interview check</div><div class=\"m-exam\"><span class=\"tag\">Interview</span><b>How do secrets reach hosts without living in plain text, and how is privilege scoped?</b><br />Secrets committed as Vault-encrypted vars/files, decrypted at run from prompt/file/CI secret with <code>no_log</code> guarding output. Privilege via <code>become</code> scoped per task (<code>become_user</code>, least-privilege sudoers), not blanket root everywhere.</div><div class=\"mark m-key\"><span class=\"tag\">Next</span>Secure automation must be trustworthy before it is triggered automatically. Next: lint, test, and Molecule quality gates.</div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">9</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 11 · Quality</div><h1 id=\"lint-check-molecule\">LINT · CHECK · MOLECULE</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">7 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHAT — Three quality gates</div><p><code>ansible-lint</code> enforces style, FQCN, and common mistakes statically. <code>--check --diff</code> dry-runs a playbook against real inventory without changing it. Molecule tests roles in ephemeral containers or VMs (create → converge → verify → destroy).</p><div class=\"panel\"><div class=\"zlabel\">Three gates before CI trusts a role</div><div class=\"frow\"><span class=\"blk b-red\">LINT<small>style + FQCN</small></span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk\">CHECK + DIFF<small>blast radius</small></span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk b-cyan\">MOLECULE<small>converge twice</small></span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk b-ok\">CI<small>same gates</small></span></div></div><div class=\"code\">ansible-lint site.yml\nansible-playbook -i inventories/staging site.yml --check --diff\nmolecule test</div><p>Molecule cycle: <code>create</code> (ephemeral host) → <code>converge</code> (apply role) → <code>verify</code> (assert state) → <code>destroy</code>. Second converge should report <code>ok</code> with zero <code>changed</code> — the idempotence proof.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">WHY — Automation multiplies mistakes</div><p>A typo in one task runs on a hundred hosts in minutes. Lint catches the typo in seconds; check-mode previews blast radius; Molecule proves the role converges twice cleanly before CI ever touches staging. Without gates, every run is a fleet experiment.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">WHERE DOES IT FIT — Quality before triggers</div><div class=\"code\">Vault-secured roles (Ch 10) → lint (seconds) → check/diff (minutes, safe) → molecule (minutes, ephemeral)\n  → CI/CD (Ch 12) runs the same gates on every push</div><p>Local order mirrors CI order: fast static checks first, expensive ephemeral tests last. What passes locally must pass identically in CI — same lint version pinned, same molecule driver.</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">10</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 11 · Quality (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"lint-check-molecule-2\">LINT · CHECK · MOLECULE</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">7 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">HOW IT WORKS — Static, dry-run, ephemeral</div><p>Lint: rule-based (<code>yaml</code>, <code>fqcn</code>, <code>name[prefix]</code>, <code>no-changed-when</code>). Pin <code>ansible-lint 6+</code> in dev requirements; <code>ansible-lint --fix</code> for safe auto-fixes. Check mode: modules report would-change without acting (<code>--check</code>); <code>--diff</code> shows file/service deltas. Command/shell tasks skip check unless <code>check_mode: true</code> is handled — another reason to prefer modules.</p><p>Molecule: <code>molecule init role acme.web -d docker</code>; <code>molecule.yml</code> defines platform, provisioner (<code>ansible_playbook</code>), verifier (<code>ansible</code> asserts). <code>verify.yml</code> asserts converged state:</p><div class=\"code\">- name: Verify\n  hosts: all\n  tasks:\n    - name: Nginx is running\n      ansible.builtin.assert:\n        that:\n          - \"'nginx' in ansible_facts.services\"</div><div class=\"taskhead\">PRACTICAL — Gate a role locally</div><div class=\"code\">COMMAND\n────────────────────────\nansible-lint roles/web/ &amp;&amp; ansible-playbook -i inventories/staging site.yml --check --diff</div><p>Meaning: static rules, then dry-run delta. Expected: lint clean, <code>--diff</code> shows only intended file lines. Any unexpected <code>changed</code> line blocks the commit.</p><div class=\"code\">COMMAND\n────────────────────────\nmolecule test</div><p>Expected: <code>create → converge (changed) → converge (ok, idempotent) → verify passed → destroy</code>. Second-converge <code>changed=0</code> is the quality signature.</p><p>Why it matters: three gates catch three bug classes (style/FQCN, blast radius, convergence). Common failure: lint <code>fqcn</code> errors on short names → rewrite to <code>ansible.builtin.*</code>.</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">11</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 11 · Quality (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"lint-check-molecule-3\">LINT · CHECK · MOLECULE</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">7 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHAT CAN FAIL</div><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely Cause</th><th>Prevention</th></tr><tr><td><code>fqcn[action-core]</code> lint errors</td><td>Short module names (<code>copy</code>, <code>template</code>)</td><td>FQCN everywhere; <code>ansible-lint --fix</code> once, then enforce</td></tr><tr><td><code>--check</code> shows nothing but real run changes</td><td><code>command</code>/<code>shell</code> tasks skip check mode</td><td>Prefer modules; add <code>check_mode: true</code> handling or <code>changed_when</code></td></tr><tr><td>Molecule verify fails</td><td>Role converged but assertion wrong</td><td>Assert observable state (service, file, port), not task output</td></tr><tr><td>Second converge still <code>changed</code></td><td>Non-idempotent content (timestamp, random)</td><td>Remove volatile rendering; retest until <code>changed=0</code></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"mark m-warn\"><span class=\"tag\">Gotcha</span>A green molecule run whose second converge still reports CHANGED\nis a failed idempotence test wearing a passing disguise.\nGate on changed=0, not just exit code.</div><div class=\"taskhead\">REAL-WORLD CONNECTION</div><p>PR pipeline: lint (30s) → check/diff against staging inventory (2min, artifact of <code>--diff</code>) → molecule (5min). Reviewer approves the <code>--diff</code> artifact, not a description. Merge to main triggers staging converge; production requires manual approval + same gates with prod inventory in check mode.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">LAB — Observe / Execute / Verify</div><p>Objective: red → green quality loop. Prereqs: <code>roles/web</code> from Ch 09, molecule + docker available.</p><ol><li>Introduce short name (<code>copy:</code>) → <code>ansible-lint roles/web/</code> → Observe <code>fqcn</code> failure</li><li>Fix to <code>ansible.builtin.copy</code> → Verify lint clean. Explain: static gate.</li><li>Run <code>--check --diff</code> → Observe planned deltas. Explain: blast-radius preview.</li><li><code>molecule test</code> → Verify second converge <code>changed=0</code> + verify passed. Explain: ephemeral convergence proof.</li></ol><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">12</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 11 · Quality (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"lint-check-molecule-4\">LINT · CHECK · MOLECULE</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">7 MIN</span></div></div><p>Failure drill: add <code>{{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }}</code> to template → molecule second converge stays <code>changed</code> → remove volatile → green.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">Interview check</div><div class=\"m-exam\"><span class=\"tag\">Interview</span><b>What does each gate prove that the others do not?</b><br />Lint proves style/FQCN correctness statically. Check/diff proves blast radius against real inventory without changing it. Molecule proves the role converges to testable state twice (idempotent) in a clean ephemeral host.</div><div class=\"mark m-key\"><span class=\"tag\">Next</span>Quality gates pass locally. Next: run them on every push and drive fleets — CI/CD and production.</div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">13</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 12 · Delivery</div><h1 id=\"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet\">CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">9 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHAT — Every push drives automation safely</div><p>CI/CD triggers <code>ansible-playbook</code> after Git push, with per-environment inventory. The pipeline runs the Ch 11 gates, previews with <code>--check --diff</code>, requires approval for prod, then converges the fleet and feeds results to observability.</p><div class=\"panel\"><div class=\"zlabel\">Every push can reach the fleet safely</div><div class=\"frow\"><span class=\"blk b-red\">GIT PUSH</span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk\">LINT + TEST</span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk\">STAGING DIFF</span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk b-chg\">APPROVAL</span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk b-ok\">PROD ROLLING</span></div></div><div class=\"code\">Git push → CI (lint) → molecule → ansible-playbook -i inventories/staging --check --diff\n  → approval → ansible-playbook -i inventories/prod → observability → feedback to Git</div><p>Project structure:</p><div class=\"code\">inventories/{staging,prod}/hosts.yml\ngroup_vars/{all,staging,prod}.yml\nhost_vars/\nroles/\nsite.yml\nansible.cfg\nrequirements.yml</div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHY — Manual runs do not survive scale</div><p>SSH-loop runs depend on who runs them, from which laptop, with which vars. CI gives one runner, pinned versions, secret-injected vault passwords, and an audit trail per commit. Staging-then-prod with identical playbooks makes promotion a change of <code>-i</code> path, not a new procedure.</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">14</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 12 · Delivery (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-2\">CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">9 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHERE DOES IT FIT — Production loop</div><div class=\"code\">Terraform provisions → Ansible configures (this series) → Docker packages → K8s orchestrates\n  → CI triggers → observability verifies → feedback to Git</div><p>Ansible owns inside-OS convergence. Execution tuning (<code>strategy</code>, <code>forks</code>, <code>serial</code>) and inventory at scale (constructed inventory, <code>group_vars</code> layering) keep that convergence fast and scoped as fleets grow.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">HOW IT WORKS — Strategies, scale, pipeline</div><p>Execution strategies: <code>linear</code> (default, lockstep per task) vs <code>free</code> (hosts race ahead). <code>forks: 20</code> caps parallelism; <code>serial: 1</code> (or <code>\"25%\"</code>) rolls hosts in batches for safe restarts. <code>ansible-inventory --graph</code> verifies selection before any run.</p><div class=\"code\">- name: Rolling web update\n  hosts: web\n  serial: 1\n  tasks:\n    - name: Render config\n      ansible.builtin.template:\n        src: nginx.conf.j2\n        dest: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf\n      notify: Restart nginx\n  handlers:\n    - name: Restart nginx\n      ansible.builtin.service:\n        name: nginx\n        state: restarted</div><p>GitHub Actions sketch: checkout → setup Python → <code>pip install ansible ansible-lint molecule</code> → <code>ansible-galaxy install -r requirements.yml</code> → lint → <code>molecule test</code> → check/diff staging (artifact) → manual approval → run prod with vault password from CI secrets.</p><p>Inventory at scale: dynamic/construction plugins generate groups from cloud tags; <code>group_vars</code> layers defaults → env → host; <code>ansible-inventory -i inventories/prod --graph --vars</code> is the pre-flight check.</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">15</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 12 · Delivery (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-3\">CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">9 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">PRACTICAL — Staging dry-run, prod rolling</div><div class=\"code\">COMMAND\n────────────────────────\nansible-inventory -i inventories/prod --graph &amp;&amp; ansible-playbook -i inventories/prod site.yml --check --diff</div><p>Meaning: prove selection, then preview deltas. Expected: graph shows <code>web</code>/<code>db</code> counts; <code>--diff</code> lists only intended lines. Any surprise line blocks promotion.</p><p>Why it matters: the <code>--diff</code> artifact is what approvers review — not a prose description. Common failure: CI env lacks vault password → decrypt error → wire CI secret to <code>--vault-password-file</code> via temp file, never echo.</p><div class=\"code\">ansible-playbook -i inventories/prod site.yml --check --diff   # reviewed artifact\nansible-playbook -i inventories/staging site.yml               # converge staging first</div><p><b>WHAT HAPPENED:</b> dry run against the prod inventory; zero changes made, full delta shown. <b>WHY IT MATTERS:</b> the diff artifact is what approvers review — not a prose description of intent. <b>COMMON FAILURE:</b> CI lacks the vault password → decrypt error; fix by wiring the secret to a file, never echoing it into logs.</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">16</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 12 · Delivery (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-4\">CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">9 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">ISSUE CATALOG — Reachability to data (1–7)</div><p>Read top to bottom: connection first, then privilege, then data, then convergence. Nine runs out of ten die in rows 1–3.</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><tr><th>#</th><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Verify</th><th>Fix</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td><code>UNREACHABLE</code></td><td>IP wrong, host down, firewall, bastion missing</td><td><code>ping</code> IP → <code>ssh user@ip</code> by hand → <code>-m ping -vvv</code></td><td>Correct <code>ansible_host</code>, open port 22, set <code>ProxyJump</code></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><code>Permission denied (publickey)</code></td><td>Key not deployed, wrong key, <code>0600</code> broken on <code>/mnt/c</code></td><td><code>ssh -i key user@ip</code> by hand</td><td><code>ssh-copy-id</code>, point <code>ansible_ssh_private_key_file</code>, keep keys in WSL home</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><code>Failed to escalate privilege</code></td><td>Sudo needs password / not granted / <code>requiretty</code></td><td><code>sudo -n true</code> on target as automation user</td><td>Scoped NOPASSWD, <code>--ask-become-pass</code>, drop <code>requiretty</code></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><code>MODULE FAILURE: python: command not found</code></td><td>No Python on minimal image</td><td><code>raw: which python3</code></td><td>Bootstrap <code>python3</code> via <code>raw</code>, set <code>ansible_python_interpreter</code></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><code>ERROR! Syntax Error</code> (YAML)</td><td>Indent mix, tabs, CRLF from Windows editor</td><td><code>yamllint</code>, <code>cat -A</code> shows <code>^M</code></td><td>2-space indent, LF endings, lint gate in CI</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><code>AnsibleUndefinedVariable</code></td><td>Typo, <code>group_vars/</code> beside wrong file</td><td><code>ansible-inventory --graph --vars</code></td><td>Fix name/path; guard with <code>| default()</code></td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Wrong value, no error (precedence)</td><td>Higher-specificity source wins silently</td><td><code>debug: var=name</code> per host</td><td>Move value to <code>host_vars/</code> or override deliberately</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">17</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 12 · Delivery (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-5\">CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">9 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">ISSUE CATALOG — Convergence and delivery (8–14)</div><p>Convergence and delivery failures behave differently: the transport works, the logic does not.</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><tr><th>#</th><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Verify</th><th>Fix</th></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><code>template error while templating string</code></td><td>Undefined var or bad filter in Jinja</td><td>Render with <code>debug</code> first</td><td><code>default()</code> guards, test filters in isolation</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Handler never runs</td><td>Task <code>OK</code> (converged) or name/<code>listen</code> mismatch</td><td>Change a var to force <code>CHANGED</code></td><td>Fix handler name, use <code>listen:</code> aliases</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><code>couldn't resolve module/action</code></td><td>Collection missing or short name</td><td><code>ansible-galaxy collection list</code></td><td>FQCN + <code>requirements.yml</code> install</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td><code>no vault secrets found</code></td><td>Password file path / <code>--vault-id</code> label wrong</td><td>Run once with <code>--ask-vault-pass</code></td><td>Wire CI secret to <code>--vault-password-file</code></td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Task always <code>CHANGED</code></td><td><code>command</code>/<code>shell</code> without guard, volatile template content</td><td>Re-run: still changed?</td><td>Prefer modules; <code>changed_when</code>/<code>creates</code>; remove timestamps from templates</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Fleet run crawls</td><td><code>linear</code> strategy, <code>forks</code> default 5, fact gathering everywhere</td><td>Time with <code>--verbose</code>, count hosts</td><td><code>forks: 20+</code>, <code>strategy: free</code> where safe, <code>gather_facts: false</code> when unused, <code>serial</code> for rolling</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>Works locally, fails in CI</td><td>Pinned versions differ, vault/SSH secrets absent in CI</td><td>Diff <code>ansible --version</code> + env both sides</td><td>Pin all versions, identical install steps, CI secret inventory</td></tr></table></div><p>Prevention stack (cheap → expensive): <code>ansible-lint</code> on every save → <code>--check --diff</code> before every real run → staging converge before prod → <code>serial</code> + approval for prod → observability on <code>changed</code> counts after.</p><div class=\"panel\"><div class=\"zlabel\">Where Ansible sits in production</div><div class=\"frow\"><span class=\"blk\">TERRAFORM<small>provisions</small></span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk b-red\">ANSIBLE<small>configures</small></span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk\">K8s / SERVICES<small>run</small></span><span class=\"harrow\">→</span><span class=\"blk b-ok\">OBSERVE<small>verify</small></span></div><p>Terraform hands addresses; Ansible owns everything inside the machine.</p></div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">18</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 12 · Delivery (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-6\">CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">9 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHAT CAN FAIL — Troubleshooting matrix</div><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Verify</th><th>Fix</th><th>Prevention</th></tr><tr><td><code>UNREACHABLE</code></td><td><code>ansible web -m ping -vvv</code></td><td>user/key/host, bastion, <code>ansible_ssh_common_args</code></td><td><code>ping</code> gate before converge in CI</td></tr><tr><td>YAML parse error</td><td><code>yamllint</code>, line number</td><td>indent/colon/quotes</td><td>lint gate blocks merge</td></tr><tr><td>Precedence surprise</td><td><code>ansible-inventory --graph --vars</code> + <code>debug</code></td><td>correct <code>group_vars/</code> placement</td><td>staging check/diff review</td></tr><tr><td>Handler silent when restart needed</td><td>task <code>OK</code> or name mismatch</td><td>force change or fix <code>listen</code></td><td><code>validate</code> + <code>--diff</code> inspection</td></tr><tr><td>Vault decrypt fail in CI</td><td>password file present?</td><td>CI secret → file → <code>--vault-password-file</code></td><td>staging pipeline runs first</td></tr><tr><td>Env mismatch (works locally, fails CI)</td><td>pinned versions?</td><td>pin <code>ansible</code>, <code>lint</code>, collections in <code>requirements*.yml</code></td><td>identical local/CI install steps</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"taskhead\">REAL-WORLD CONNECTION</div><p>End-to-end: Terraform applies infra → outputs inventory → CI runs Ansible staging converge → <code>--diff</code> approved → prod rolling converge (<code>serial: \"25%\"</code>) → Prometheus <code>changed</code>-count drop and service health confirm → Grafana dashboard links back to commit SHA. Drift next week re-runs the same commit — <code>CHANGED</code> hosts are the drift report.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">LAB — Observe / Execute / Verify</div><p>Objective: promote same commit staging → prod. Prereqs: <code>inventories/staging</code>, <code>inventories/prod</code>.</p><ol><li><code>ansible-inventory -i inventories/staging --graph</code> → Observe selection</li><li><code>--check --diff</code> staging → Execute, capture artifact → Verify intended deltas only</li><li>Converge staging → Verify <code>changed</code> then re-run <code>changed=0</code></li><li>Repeat check/diff against prod → approval → rolling converge <code>serial: 1</code>.</li></ol><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">19</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 12 · Delivery (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-7\">CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">9 MIN</span></div></div><p>Failure drill: point prod run at staging inventory → graph mismatch → abort via selection check before converge.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">Interview check</div><div class=\"m-exam\"><span class=\"tag\">Interview</span><b>How does a commit safely reach production fleet?</b><br />Push runs lint → molecule → staging check/diff (reviewed artifact) → staging converge → prod check/diff → approval → rolling prod converge with vault secrets from CI, verified by inventory graph and observability — same playbook, different <code>-i</code> path.</div><div class=\"mark m-key\"><span class=\"tag\">Next</span>Fleet delivery works. Next: the orchestration edge — delegation, async, blocks, and running subsets.</div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">20</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 13 · Edge</div><h1 id=\"delegation-async-blocks-tags\">DELEGATION · ASYNC · BLOCKS · TAGS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHAT — Orchestration controls</div><p><code>delegate_to</code> runs a task on a different host than the play target. <code>local_action</code> runs on the control node. <code>async</code>/<code>poll</code> runs long tasks without blocking. <code>block</code>/<code>rescue</code>/<code>always</code> groups tasks with recovery. <code>tags</code> selects subsets.</p><div class=\"panel\"><div class=\"zlabel\">Run elsewhere, run long, run safe</div><div class=\"frow\"><span class=\"blk\">DELEGATE_TO<small>act on another host</small></span><span class=\"blk\">ASYNC + POLL<small>long jobs</small></span><span class=\"blk b-ok\">BLOCK / RESCUE<small>recover</small></span><span class=\"blk\">TAGS + LIMIT<small>subsets</small></span></div></div><div class=\"code\">- name: Migrate with recovery\n  block:\n    - name: Run migration\n      ansible.builtin.command: /opt/migrate.sh\n      async: 600\n      poll: 10\n  rescue:\n    - name: Roll back\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg: \"migrate failed, rolling back\"\n  always:\n    - name: Ensure app started\n      ansible.builtin.service:\n        name: app\n        state: started\n\n- name: Drain from load balancer\n  ansible.builtin.uri:\n    url: \"http://lb/drain?host={{ inventory_hostname }}\"\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  run_once: true</div><p>Run subsets: <code>ansible-playbook site.yml --tags deploy --limit web</code>.</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">21</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 13 · Edge (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"delegation-async-blocks-tags-2\">DELEGATION · ASYNC · BLOCKS · TAGS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">WHY — Real runs need escape hatches</div><p>Migrations fail mid-fleet; long jobs exceed SSH timeouts; load balancers must drain one host at a time; operators need to run only <code>deploy</code> tags at 2am. Without these controls every edge case becomes a separate playbook — with them, one playbook handles happy path, slow path, and failure path.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">WHERE DOES IT FIT — Edge after production</div><div class=\"code\">CI/CD delivery (Ch 12) runs the standard path → this chapter handles the non-standard:\n  different host (delegate) → long job (async) → failure (block/rescue) → subset (tags/limit)</div><p>These are execution modifiers, not new declarative models. Teach them last because each assumes the learner already reads plays, data flow, handlers, and rolling updates fluently.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">HOW IT WORKS — Where, how long, what if, which</div><p>Delegation: task executes on <code>delegate_to</code> host but <code>inventory_hostname</code> still refers to original target — use for LB/API calls about the target. <code>run_once: true</code> + <code>delegate_to: localhost</code> runs a single API call, not once per host. Async: <code>async: 600</code> (max seconds) + <code>poll: 10</code> (check interval); <code>poll: 0</code> fires and continues (collect with <code>async_status</code> later). Blocks: <code>rescue</code> runs only if <code>block</code> fails; <code>always</code> runs regardless — the try/except/finally of playbooks. Tags: <code>tags: [deploy, never]</code>; <code>--tags</code>, <code>--skip-tags</code>, <code>--list-tags</code>; <code>never</code> tags run only when requested.</p><div class=\"code\">- name: Long firmware job\n  ansible.builtin.command: /opt/flash.sh\n  async: 1800\n  poll: 0\n  register: flash_job\n\n- name: Wait for firmware\n  ansible.builtin.async_status:\n    jid: \"{{ flash_job.ansible_job_id }}\"\n  register: flash_result\n  until: flash_result.finished\n  retries: 60\n  delay: 30</div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">22</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 13 · Edge (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"delegation-async-blocks-tags-3\">DELEGATION · ASYNC · BLOCKS · TAGS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">PRACTICAL — Prove rescue + async</div><div class=\"code\">COMMAND\n────────────────────────\nansible-playbook -i inventory.ini rescue-demo.yml --tags migrate</div><p>Expected: failing <code>block</code> task → <code>rescue</code> debug runs → <code>always</code> service start runs → play recap <code>failed=0</code> (recovered) with rescue visible. Remove <code>rescue</code> → recap <code>failed=1</code> — proves recovery changed the outcome.</p><p>Why it matters: rescue converts fleet-stopping failures into logged recoveries with service guarantees. Common failure: <code>delegate_to</code> without <code>run_once</code> on LB drain → N duplicate drains → add <code>run_once: true</code>.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">WHAT CAN FAIL</div><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely Cause</th><th>Prevention</th></tr><tr><td>LB drained N times</td><td><code>delegate_to</code> runs per host</td><td><code>run_once: true</code> for singleton API calls</td></tr><tr><td>Async job lost</td><td><code>poll: 0</code> without <code>async_status</code> follow-up</td><td><code>until/retries/delay</code> poller task with <code>ansible_job_id</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>rescue</code> masks real failure</td><td>Over-broad rescue hides root cause</td><td>Rescue logs + re-raises (<code>fail:</code>) when unrecoverable; alert, not silence</td></tr><tr><td><code>--tags</code> runs nothing</td><td>Tag typo or <code>never</code> tag not requested</td><td><code>--list-tags</code> before run; audit tag names in review</td></tr><tr><td><code>command</code> always <code>CHANGED</code> in block</td><td>Imperative task without guard</td><td><code>changed_when</code>, <code>creates</code>/<code>removes</code>, or <code>failed_when: rc not in [0]</code></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"mark m-warn\"><span class=\"tag\">Gotcha</span><code>rescue</code> is not exception forgiveness — it is a second playbook branch.\nIf rescue cannot actually restore service, fail loudly with ansible.builtin.fail\nso CI and observability see red, not a polite debug message.</div><div class=\"taskhead\">REAL-WORLD CONNECTION</div><p>Zero-downtime deploy: <code>serial: 1</code> → <code>delegate_to: localhost</code> drains host from LB (<code>run_once</code> per batch item) → deploy + handler restart → <code>uri</code> health check with <code>until/retries</code> → re-add to LB in <code>always</code>. <code>--tags rollback</code> runs only the restore branch. Same playbook deploys, verifies, and recovers — the runbook and the automation are one file.</p><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">23</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Chapter 13 · Edge (cont.)</div><h1 id=\"delegation-async-blocks-tags-4\">DELEGATION · ASYNC · BLOCKS · TAGS</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">8 MIN</span></div></div><div class=\"taskhead\">LAB — Observe / Execute / Verify</div><p>Objective: drain → deploy → verify → recover. Prereqs: <code>rescue-demo.yml</code> with block/rescue/always + drain task.</p><ol><li>Run with <code>--list-tags</code> → Observe available subsets</li><li>Run <code>--tags migrate</code> with failing migration → Verify rescue + always both ran, recap recovered</li><li>Convert long task to <code>async: 300 / poll: 0</code> + <code>async_status</code> poller → Verify non-blocking completion</li><li>Add <code>delegate_to: localhost / run_once: true</code> to drain → Verify single drain for whole batch.</li></ol><p>Failure drill: remove <code>run_once</code> → observe duplicate drains → restore; remove <code>rescue</code> → observe hard failure → restore.</p><div class=\"taskhead\">Interview check</div><div class=\"m-exam\"><span class=\"tag\">Interview</span><b>When do you delegate, async, block, or tag?</b><br />Delegate when the action concerns another host (LB, API, control node). Async when the job outlasts comfortable SSH blocking. Block/rescue/always when failure needs scoped recovery with guaranteed cleanup. Tags + limit when the operator must run a named subset safely.</div><div class=\"mark m-key\"><span class=\"tag\">Next</span>Series complete: foundations declare state, engineering varies and organizes it, production secures, tests, delivers, and recovers it. Return to Ch 01 decision tree for the next fleet.</div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">24</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet\"><div class=\"pghead\"><div class=\"hrow\"><div><div class=\"kick\">Appendix · Cheatsheet</div><h1 id=\"cheatsheet-secure-to-deliver\">CHEATSHEET — SECURE TO DELIVER</h1></div><span class=\"hmeta\">FINALE</span></div></div><div class=\"grid2\"><div><h3 id=\"a-vault-and-become\"><span>A</span> Vault and Become</h3><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Need</th><th>Command</th></tr><tr><td>Encrypt file</td><td><code>ansible-vault encrypt</code></td></tr><tr><td>Inline secret</td><td><code>encrypt_string --name</code></td></tr><tr><td>Run</td><td><code>--ask-vault-pass</code> / password-file</td></tr><tr><td>Scope root</td><td><code>become: true</code> per task</td></tr></table></div></div><div><h3 id=\"b-gates-and-delivery\"><span>B</span> Gates and Delivery</h3><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Need</th><th>Command</th></tr><tr><td>Lint</td><td><code>ansible-lint site.yml</code></td></tr><tr><td>Preview</td><td><code>--check --diff</code></td></tr><tr><td>Ephemeral</td><td><code>molecule test</code></td></tr><tr><td>Subset</td><td><code>--tags x --limit y</code></td></tr></table></div></div></div><div class=\"frow\"><span>● OK — converged, no change</span><span>◐ CHANGED — converged, did change</span><span> FAILED — did not converge</span></div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">25</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div><div class=\"sheet cover\"><div><div class=\"ckick\">End Production · Vol 3</div><div>SERIES COMPLETE</div><p>Declare state, vary it per host, secure it, test it, deliver it — and recover.</p></div><div class=\"folio\"><span>Production · Vol 3</span><span class=\"fnum\">26</span><span><span class=\"rok\">ok</span> <span class=\"rchg\">changed</span> failed=0</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">TOC</a></span></div></div>","toc":[{"id":"productionansible","text":"PRODUCTIONANSIBLE","level":1},{"id":"table-of-contents","text":"TABLE OF CONTENTS","level":1},{"id":"vault-become-secrets","text":"VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS","level":1},{"id":"vault-become-secrets-2","text":"VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS","level":1},{"id":"vault-become-secrets-3","text":"VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS","level":1},{"id":"vault-become-secrets-4","text":"VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS","level":1},{"id":"vault-become-secrets-5","text":"VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS","level":1},{"id":"vault-become-secrets-6","text":"VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS","level":1},{"id":"vault-become-secrets-7","text":"VAULT · BECOME · SECRETS","level":1},{"id":"lint-check-molecule","text":"LINT · CHECK · MOLECULE","level":1},{"id":"lint-check-molecule-2","text":"LINT · CHECK · MOLECULE","level":1},{"id":"lint-check-molecule-3","text":"LINT · CHECK · MOLECULE","level":1},{"id":"lint-check-molecule-4","text":"LINT · CHECK · MOLECULE","level":1},{"id":"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet","text":"CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET","level":1},{"id":"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-2","text":"CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET","level":1},{"id":"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-3","text":"CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET","level":1},{"id":"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-4","text":"CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET","level":1},{"id":"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-5","text":"CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET","level":1},{"id":"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-6","text":"CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET","level":1},{"id":"ci-cd-commit-to-fleet-7","text":"CI/CD — COMMIT TO FLEET","level":1},{"id":"delegation-async-blocks-tags","text":"DELEGATION · ASYNC · BLOCKS · TAGS","level":1},{"id":"delegation-async-blocks-tags-2","text":"DELEGATION · ASYNC · BLOCKS · TAGS","level":1},{"id":"delegation-async-blocks-tags-3","text":"DELEGATION · ASYNC · BLOCKS · TAGS","level":1},{"id":"delegation-async-blocks-tags-4","text":"DELEGATION · ASYNC · BLOCKS · TAGS","level":1},{"id":"cheatsheet-secure-to-deliver","text":"CHEATSHEET — SECURE TO DELIVER","level":1},{"id":"a-vault-and-become","text":"A Vault and Become","level":3},{"id":"b-gates-and-delivery","text":"B Gates and Delivery","level":3}],"words":4583,"assets":[]};